<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Multi-Tier Cloud Application'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Multi-Tier Cloud-Native Application</h1>
  <p>EC2 + S3 frontend, Lambda serverless backend, DynamoDB for orders, RDS for relational data, SNS notifications, and scoped IAM roles per service.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>EC2</span><span>Lambda</span><span>DynamoDB</span><span>RDS</span><span>SNS</span><span>S3</span><span>IAM</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/multi-tier-app.png" alt="Multi-Tier Application Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates a <strong>cloud-native multi-tier architecture</strong> combining traditional EC2 hosting with serverless backend services, showcasing real-world enterprise patterns.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> Static files stored in S3, synced to EC2 running Apache HTTPD.</li>
      <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Serverless Lambda function handling order processing.</li>
      <li><strong>Databases:</strong> DynamoDB for orders, RDS (MariaDB) for relational data.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> SNS sends email alerts on new orders.</li>
      <li><strong>Security:</strong> Scoped IAM policies + Security Groups per service.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🖥️ Frontend Tier</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>S3</strong> — Stores HTML/CSS/JS files</li>
          <li><strong>EC2 + Apache</strong> — Serves static content</li>
          <li>Files synced from S3 to <code>/var/www/html</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>⚡ Backend Tier</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Lambda</strong> — Processes orders serverlessly</li>
          <li><strong>DynamoDB</strong> — NoSQL order storage</li>
          <li><strong>SNS</strong> — Email notifications on orders</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🗄️ Data Tier</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>RDS MariaDB</strong> — Relational data practice</li>
          <li>EC2 SG allows SSH + HTTP only</li>
          <li>RDS SG allows MySQL from EC2 only</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Created S3 bucket, uploaded frontend files, created <strong>scoped IAM policies</strong> for each service.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Created <strong>DynamoDB table</strong> and <strong>SNS topic</strong> with email subscription.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Created <strong>Lambda function</strong> with DynamoDB write + SNS publish permissions.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Launched EC2, installed Apache, synced S3 files to serve the frontend.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Created <strong>RDS MariaDB</strong> in VPC, configured Security Groups, tested EC2→RDS connectivity.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Built a <strong>multi-tier architecture</strong> combining EC2 and serverless components.</li>
      <li>Created <strong>granular IAM policies</strong> following least-privilege principle.</li>
      <li>Implemented <strong>Lambda + DynamoDB + SNS</strong> for serverless order processing.</li>
      <li>Understood <strong>when to use DynamoDB vs RDS</strong> based on data access patterns.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>S3 sync</strong> for frontend deployments to EC2.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
